From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:56:40 +0000
Subject: src: avoid scavenges while generating a predictable snapshot

--predictable does not cover V8's minor GC task. Once the young
generation is 80% full, V8 posts a foreground task that scavenges
early, and whether node's event loop runs it before the next young
allocation fails depends on thread timing. A scavenge at a different
point leaves objects on different pages, so read-only promotion (which
walks the heap in page order) copies them into read-only space in a
different order. That changes the read-only snapshot, its checksum, and
every code cache entry that records the checksum, so node_mksnapshot
produced different bytes from run to run on a busy machine.

Give the snapshot-building process a 32MB semi-space so building the
built-in snapshot never needs a scavenge. Semi-space sizes are left out
of V8's flag hash, so the snapshot and its code cache stay compatible
with runtimes that use the default sizes. Runtime flags are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/node.cc b/src/node.cc
index cda7acb7c01f66306ff5f4524cbbaecac15bf3e5..6913bcd121579dd07a6075f2874264aee4d622df 100644
--- a/src/node.cc
+++ b/src/node.cc
@@ -916,6 +916,17 @@ static ExitCode InitializeNodeWithArgsInternal(
       per_process::cli_options->per_isolate->build_snapshot) {
     v8::V8::SetFlagsFromString("--predictable");
     v8::V8::SetFlagsFromString("--random_seed=42");
+    // --predictable does not cover V8's minor GC task: once the young
+    // generation is 80% full, V8 posts a foreground task that scavenges
+    // early, and when the event loop runs it depends on thread timing. A
+    // scavenge at a different point lays the heap out differently, which
+    // changes the order objects are promoted to read-only space in and so
+    // the snapshot bytes. Make the young generation large enough that the
+    // built-in snapshot never needs a scavenge. Semi-space sizes are not
+    // part of V8's flag hash, so the snapshot and its code cache stay valid
+    // for runtimes using the default sizes.
+    v8::V8::SetFlagsFromString("--min-semi-space-size=32");
+    v8::V8::SetFlagsFromString("--max-semi-space-size=32");
   }
 
